  "core_engineering_findings": [
    "Repair locality and downstream efficacy are empirically separable across all four frozen groups: all 45 valid paired interventions preserved unrelated structure, while downstream effects remained heterogeneous.",
    "One-shot local repair frequently does not close the process: persistence occurred in 18/45 valid pairs and mixed effects in 15/45.",
    "Repair-generated process regeneration was observed in 5/45 valid pairs and in every group G2-G5.",
    "Clean targeted suppression/redirection occurred in 7/45 valid pairs; direct target change occurred in 27/45, so direct local change is not equivalent to downstream closure.",
    "T1 is strongly persistence-dominated in this frozen sample: 14 persistence, 1 mixed effect and 1 regeneration across 16 valid T1 pairs.",
    "T2 is the principal boundary/regeneration family: 13 valid pairs plus 3 boundaries, with 8 mixed effects, 4 regeneration effects and 1 targeted redirection.",
    "T3 remains heterogeneous: across 16 valid pairs there are 3 targeted suppressions, 3 targeted redirections, 6 mixed effects and 4 persistence effects.",
    "Boundary observations are not negative repair samples and must not be converted into preferred outcomes by rerun, scope expansion or synthetic state repair.",
    "The engineering control plane itself requires process-integrity protection: the G3 duplicate-execution incident motivated pre-provider atomic execution claims and explicit canonical-attempt accounting."
  ],
